{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"# Source-local evidence delta\n\n## SOURCE AXIOM\nVERSION 968512cff889b2c6ebfd5c0e9a732ea29a12a9659fffbaa4ea010aba7cb4b775\n\n### REQUIREMENTS\nQ01: Establishes distinct authority boundaries for quality hold/release, recall initiation, regulatory notice, and procurement execution. Q10: Defines handoff validity requirements for recovery candidates, affected lots, and assay plans. Q12: Mandates separation of detection, recommendation, authorization, execution, verification, and closure functions.\n\n### FINDINGS\nQuality unit holds/releases lots; incident commander coordinates recovery; regulator receives mandatory notice; procurement executes approved supplier choices [AXIOM]. Field recall requires quality-unit recommendation plus accountable-executive authorization. Emergency purchasing does not waive validated process, sterility, labeling, or traceability controls [AXIOM]. Shift handoffs are valid only when receiving owners acknowledge identical recovery-candidate, affected-lot, and assay-plan versions; unacknowledged handoffs block closure [AXIOM]. Operational evidence (AUTH-000 to AUTH-047) shows approval status across quality-unit, incident-commander, regulator, and procurement roles with revisions r2-r4. Records AUTH-000, AUTH-013, AUTH-026, AUTH-039 show hold status; others current [AXIOM].\n\n### QUALIFICATIONS AND CONFLICTS\nHazard evidence from BRAMBLE informs hold/release but does not create legal authority [AXIOM]. Supplier or model-authored evidence slots are advisory only, never recall or release authority [AXIOM]. Emergency purchasing authority explicitly excludes waiving validated controls [AXIOM]. No conflicts observed within AXIOM bytes; role separations remain consistent across all 48 records.\n\n### UNKNOWNS AND REOPEN CONDITIONS\nUnspecified: exact criteria triggering \"hold\" vs \"current\" status transitions for AUTH records; specific evidence required to retire each hold state per decision constraints [AXIOM]. Reopen if: any handoff lacks version acknowledgment of recovery-candidate, affected-lot, or assay-plan; if quality-unit release decision is substituted by other roles; if emergency purchasing waives validated controls.\n\n## SOURCE BRAMBLE\nVERSION b5887292924f964689a1d92f2f9d7592183070bd5501148d5be30f58aa1619d4\n\n### REQUIREMENTS\nQ02: Defines hazard thresholds, lot/line holds, investigation triggers, and release rules. Q11: Specifies sampling context for M41 samples and assay-drift probability interpretation. Q12: Requires preservation of exact units and meanings for thresholds, observed values, and probabilities.\n\n### FINDINGS\nAlert threshold: 0.25 EU/mL; rejection limit: 0.50 EU/mL [BRAMBLE]. Two validated M41 samples measured 0.31 and 0.34 EU/mL; lot remains held during open water-loop investigation despite values below rejection limit [BRAMBLE]. Stability modeling assigns 41 percent probability of assay drift after eighteen hours; this is not humidity, defect prevalence, or readiness score [BRAMBLE]. Operational evidence (QUAL-000 to QUAL-047) spans lot-M41, line-A, line-B, water-loop across revisions r2-r4. Hold status appears in QUAL-000 (lot-M41, 0.2 EU/mL), QUAL-013 (line-A, 3.1 EU/mL), QUAL-026 (line-B, 3.0 EU/mL), QUAL-039 (water-loop, 2.8 EU/mL) [BRAMBLE].\n\n### QUALIFICATIONS AND CONFLICTS\nValues and units must not be converted into hours, percent, or temperature [BRAMBLE]. HEATH defines valid confirmation/release rounds; DRIFT and EMBER changes invalidate prior line samples for changed candidates [BRAMBLE]. NORTH identified prior mismatched lot revisions in particulate/endotoxin reporting [BRAMBLE]. No internal conflicts; thresholds remain distinct from observed values.\n\n### UNKNOWNS AND REOPEN CONDITIONS\nUnspecified: exact mechanism linking 41% drift probability to hold duration; specific conditions starting, holding, expanding, or retiring lot/line controls per decision constraints [BRAMBLE]. Reopen if: any water-loop investigation finding changes; if DRIFT or EMBER candidate versions change; if M41 sample values approach rejection limit (0.50 EU/mL); if HEATH confirmation rounds are invalidated."}}],"created":1787701308,"model":"Qwen3.8-27B-AD-IQ2_S.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10434-7e4c0a968","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":1010,"prompt_tokens":4234,"total_tokens":5244,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-W72aEy9xh3fKa8JlItNMUA5hZhLqcplw","__verbose":{"index":0,"content":"# Source-local evidence delta\n\n## SOURCE AXIOM\nVERSION 968512cff889b2c6ebfd5c0e9a732ea29a12a9659fffbaa4ea010aba7cb4b775\n\n### REQUIREMENTS\nQ01: Establishes distinct authority boundaries for quality hold/release, recall initiation, regulatory notice, and procurement execution. Q10: Defines handoff validity requirements for recovery candidates, affected lots, and assay plans. Q12: Mandates separation of detection, recommendation, authorization, execution, verification, and closure functions.\n\n### FINDINGS\nQuality unit holds/releases lots; incident commander coordinates recovery; regulator receives mandatory notice; procurement executes approved supplier choices [AXIOM]. Field recall requires quality-unit recommendation plus accountable-executive authorization. Emergency purchasing does not waive validated process, sterility, labeling, or traceability controls [AXIOM]. Shift handoffs are valid only when receiving owners acknowledge identical recovery-candidate, affected-lot, and assay-plan versions; unacknowledged handoffs block closure [AXIOM]. Operational evidence (AUTH-000 to AUTH-047) shows approval status across quality-unit, incident-commander, regulator, and procurement roles with revisions r2-r4. Records AUTH-000, AUTH-013, AUTH-026, AUTH-039 show hold status; others current [AXIOM].\n\n### QUALIFICATIONS AND CONFLICTS\nHazard evidence from BRAMBLE informs hold/release but does not create legal authority [AXIOM]. Supplier or model-authored evidence slots are advisory only, never recall or release authority [AXIOM]. Emergency purchasing authority explicitly excludes waiving validated controls [AXIOM]. No conflicts observed within AXIOM bytes; role separations remain consistent across all 48 records.\n\n### UNKNOWNS AND REOPEN CONDITIONS\nUnspecified: exact criteria triggering \"hold\" vs \"current\" status transitions for AUTH records; specific evidence required to retire each hold state per decision constraints [AXIOM]. Reopen if: any handoff lacks version acknowledgment of recovery-candidate, affected-lot, or assay-plan; if quality-unit release decision is substituted by other roles; if emergency purchasing waives validated controls.\n\n## SOURCE BRAMBLE\nVERSION b5887292924f964689a1d92f2f9d7592183070bd5501148d5be30f58aa1619d4\n\n### REQUIREMENTS\nQ02: Defines hazard thresholds, lot/line holds, investigation triggers, and release rules. Q11: Specifies sampling context for M41 samples and assay-drift probability interpretation. Q12: Requires preservation of exact units and meanings for thresholds, observed values, and probabilities.\n\n### FINDINGS\nAlert threshold: 0.25 EU/mL; rejection limit: 0.50 EU/mL [BRAMBLE]. Two validated M41 samples measured 0.31 and 0.34 EU/mL; lot remains held during open water-loop investigation despite values below rejection limit [BRAMBLE]. Stability modeling assigns 41 percent probability of assay drift after eighteen hours; this is not humidity, defect prevalence, or readiness score [BRAMBLE]. Operational evidence (QUAL-000 to QUAL-047) spans lot-M41, line-A, line-B, water-loop across revisions r2-r4. Hold status appears in QUAL-000 (lot-M41, 0.2 EU/mL), QUAL-013 (line-A, 3.1 EU/mL), QUAL-026 (line-B, 3.0 EU/mL), QUAL-039 (water-loop, 2.8 EU/mL) [BRAMBLE].\n\n### QUALIFICATIONS AND CONFLICTS\nValues and units must not be converted into hours, percent, or temperature [BRAMBLE]. HEATH defines valid confirmation/release rounds; DRIFT and EMBER changes invalidate prior line samples for changed candidates [BRAMBLE]. NORTH identified prior mismatched lot revisions in particulate/endotoxin reporting [BRAMBLE]. No internal conflicts; thresholds remain distinct from observed values.\n\n### UNKNOWNS AND REOPEN CONDITIONS\nUnspecified: exact mechanism linking 41% drift probability to hold duration; specific conditions starting, holding, expanding, or retiring lot/line controls per decision constraints [BRAMBLE]. Reopen if: any water-loop investigation finding changes; if DRIFT or EMBER candidate versions change; if M41 sample values approach rejection limit (0.50 EU/mL); if HEATH confirmation rounds are invalidated.","tokens":[],"id_slot":0,"stop":true,"model":"Qwen3.8-27B-AD-IQ2_S.gguf","tokens_predicted":1010,"tokens_evaluated":4234,"generation_settings":{"seed":427032,"temperature":0.699999988079071,"dynatemp_range":0.0,"dynatemp_exponent":1.0,"top_k":20,"top_p":0.800000011920929,"min_p":0.0,"top_n_sigma":-1.0,"xtc_probability":0.0,"xtc_threshold":0.10000000149011612,"typical_p":1.0,"repeat_last_n":64,"repeat_penalty":1.0,"presence_penalty":1.5,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"dry_multiplier":0.0,"dry_base":1.75,"dry_allowed_length":2,"dry_penalty_last_n":64,"dry_sequence_breakers":["\n",":","\"","*"],"mirostat":0,"mirostat_tau":5.0,"mirostat_eta":0.10000000149011612,"adaptive_target":-1.0,"adaptive_decay":0.8999999761581421,"stop":[],"max_tokens":1800,"n_predict":1800,"n_keep":0,"n_discard":0,"ignore_eos":false,"stream":false,"logit_bias":[],"n_probs":0,"min_keep":0,"grammar":"","grammar_lazy":false,"grammar_triggers":[],"preserved_tokens":[248058,248059,248068,248069],"chat_format":"peg-native","reasoning_format":"deepseek","reasoning_in_content":false,"generation_prompt":"<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","samplers":["penalties","dry","top_n_sigma","top_k","typ_p","top_p","min_p","xtc","temperature"],"speculative.types":"none","timings_per_token":false,"post_sampling_probs":false,"backend_sampling":false,"lora":[]},"prompt":"<|im_start|>system\n# SOURCE_LOCAL_EVIDENCE_DELTA maintenance mode\n\nReturn only bounded Markdown beginning exactly `# Source-local evidence delta`. Emit exactly\none `## SOURCE <ID>` block for every source in the current exact batch and no\nother source. The next line must be `VERSION <sha256>`. Each block must contain,\nin order: ### REQUIREMENTS, ### FINDINGS, ### QUALIFICATIONS AND CONFLICTS, ### UNKNOWNS AND REOPEN CONDITIONS.\n\nTransform only the supplied exact source bytes. Preserve units, probabilities,\nversions, qualifications, contradictions, and task requirement links Q01-Q12.\nThe output is lossy, source-bound task work. It cannot replace the global\nregister, authorize readiness, recommend submission, or edit absent source\nslots. Hard total limit: 1500 tokens; hard per-source limit:\n650 tokens. Allowed exact bindings:\n{\"AXIOM\":\"968512cff889b2c6ebfd5c0e9a732ea29a12a9659fffbaa4ea010aba7cb4b775\",\"BRAMBLE\":\"b5887292924f964689a1d92f2f9d7592183070bd5501148d5be30f58aa1619d4\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Authoritative task\n\n# Authoritative task — Meridian sterile-infusion recovery decision\n\nMeridian Therapeutics must recover production and allocate sterile infusion\nbags during a quality hold and regional shortage. Build and maintain the exact\ncandidate files, then propose submission only when the package is genuinely\nready for independent review.\n\nThe world contains sixteen exact, versioned source objects with opaque IDs.\nThe catalog titles help navigation but do not supply source findings. Read the\nbytes needed for the work. Cite sources as `[SOURCE_ID]`.\n\n## Required exact work\n\nMaintain `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md` as a source/version-slot evidence\nregister. Each slot must remain local to its bound source, preserve important\nqualifications and uncertainty, and identify relevant requirements Q01–Q12.\nThe register is model-authored, lossy, and non-authoritative. It may guide work\nbut cannot prove readiness.\n\nConstruct `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md` as a 1,400–2,000-word\nMeridian Sterile-Infusion Recovery Decision with exactly the declared section\nheadings. It must use at least twelve distinct sources and integrate—not merely\nlist—the governing relationships.\n\nAddress all twelve requirement groups:\n\n- Q01 — quality, recall, procurement, execution, and closure authority;\n- Q02 — hazard thresholds, lot/line holds, investigation, and release rules;\n- Q03 — time-bound demand, overlap, uncertainty, and equitable allocation;\n- Q04 — validated manufacturing capacity and shared constraints;\n- Q05 — component qualification, supplier timing, inspection, and release;\n- Q06 — usable cold-chain distribution, routes, custody, and acknowledgment;\n- Q07 — clinical priority, substitution, pharmacy review, and protected cohorts;\n- Q08 — qualified staffing, utilities, safety, duty, relief, and continuity;\n- Q09 — lot genealogy, facility/patient linkage, privacy, retention, and deletion;\n- Q10 — seventy-two-hour execution, owners, sequencing, contingencies, and cost;\n- Q11 — candidate-bound sampling, controls, checks, currentness, repair, and recheck;\n- Q12 — explicit blockers, falsifiers, independent readiness, and closure evidence.\n\n## Relationship rules\n\nPreserve exact units and distinguish alerts from rejection limits, probabilities\nfrom observed values, targets from observed performance, nominal capacity from\nshared validated throughput, registry coverage from demand, dispatch from usable\ndelivery, and mechanical checking from independent readiness. A change to a\nline, sterilizer, component, supplier, route, shift, lot chain, sample plan, or\ncandidate can make earlier evidence stale.\n\nThe decision must state owners, inputs, resources, timings, dependencies,\neffects, observations, contingencies, retirement conditions, and evidence that\nwould falsify important claims. Do not infer that a green format check, source\nslot, mutation, or submission establishes safety or completeness.\n\n\n# Prior slots for only the current sources\n\n## PRIOR SLOT AXIOM\nnone\n## PRIOR SLOT BRAMBLE\nnone\n\n# Newly externalized exact source observations\n\n## EXACT RESULT RESULT-001\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:AXIOM:1-70+BRAMBLE:1-70\",\"object_version\":\"ff871ee116738e7a5fb554504292c6e60d76a6af51af846facf0405472cd8945\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"AXIOM\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"BRAMBLE\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8382}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"AXIOM\",\"source_path\":\"sources/AXIOM_AUTHORITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"968512cff889b2c6ebfd5c0e9a732ea29a12a9659fffbaa4ea010aba7cb4b775\",\"source_size_bytes\":4232,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Emergency manufacturing, recall, and release authority\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe independent quality unit places or releases a lot hold. The incident commander coordinates recovery, the regulator receives mandatory notice, and procurement executes an approved supplier choice; none may substitute for the quality release decision.\nA field recall begins on quality-unit recommendation and accountable-executive authorization. Emergency purchasing authority does not waive validated process, sterility, labeling, or traceability controls.\nA shift handoff is valid only when the receiving owner acknowledges the same recovery-candidate, affected-lot, and assay-plan versions. An unacknowledged handoff blocks closure.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nHazard evidence from BRAMBLE and HEATH informs the hold or release but does not itself create legal authority. Every manufacturing, allocation, and checker effect must bind one candidate version.\nA supplier or model-authored evidence slot is advisory work, never recall or release authority.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| AUTH-000 | quality-unit | r2 | 1.0 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-001 | incident-commander | r2 | 1.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-002 | regulator | r2 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-003 | procurement | r2 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-004 | quality-unit | r2 | 3.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-005 | incident-commander | r2 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-006 | regulator | r2 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-007 | procurement | r2 | 2.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-008 | quality-unit | r2 | 3.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-009 | incident-commander | r2 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-010 | regulator | r2 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-011 | procurement | r2 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-012 | quality-unit | r2 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-013 | incident-commander | r2 | 3.9 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-014 | regulator | r2 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-015 | procurement | r2 | 2.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-016 | quality-unit | r3 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-017 | incident-commander | r3 | 3.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-018 | regulator | r3 | 1.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-019 | procurement | r3 | 1.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-020 | quality-unit | r3 | 2.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-021 | incident-commander | r3 | 3.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-022 | regulator | r3 | 4.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-023 | procurement | r3 | 1.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-024 | quality-unit | r3 | 2.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-025 | incident-commander | r3 | 3.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-026 | regulator | r3 | 3.7 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-027 | procurement | r3 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-028 | quality-unit | r3 | 2.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-029 | incident-commander | r3 | 2.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-030 | regulator | r3 | 3.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-031 | procurement | r3 | 1.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-032 | quality-unit | r4 | 1.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-033 | incident-commander | r4 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-034 | regulator | r4 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-035 | procurement | r4 | 3.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-036 | quality-unit | r4 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-037 | incident-commander | r4 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-038 | regulator | r4 | 2.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-039 | procurement | r4 | 3.5 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-040 | quality-unit | r4 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-041 | incident-commander | r4 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-042 | regulator | r4 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-043 | procurement | r4 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-044 | quality-unit | r4 | 3.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-045 | incident-commander | r4 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-046 | regulator | r4 | 2.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-047 | procurement | r4 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nSeparate detection, recommendation, authorization, execution, verification, and closure.\nName the accountable owner and exact evidence needed to retire each hold.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"BRAMBLE\",\"source_path\":\"sources/BRAMBLE_CONTAMINATION.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"b5887292924f964689a1d92f2f9d7592183070bd5501148d5be30f58aa1619d4\",\"source_size_bytes\":3686,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Endotoxin, particulate, and assay-drift thresholds\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe alert threshold is 0.25 endotoxin units per milliliter and the rejection limit is 0.50 EU/mL. Values and units must not be converted into hours, percent, or temperature.\nTwo validated M41 samples measured 0.31 and 0.34 EU/mL. The lot remains held while the water-loop investigation is open even though neither value reaches the rejection limit.\nCurrent stability modeling assigns a 41 percent probability of assay drift after eighteen hours. That probability is not humidity, defect prevalence, or a readiness score.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nHEATH defines valid confirmation and release rounds; DRIFT and EMBER changes make prior line samples stale for the changed candidate.\nNORTH found that particulate inspection and endotoxin sampling were previously reported under mismatched lot revisions.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| QUAL-000 | lot-M41 | r2 | 0.2 | EU/mL | hold |\n| QUAL-001 | line-A | r2 | 0.9 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-002 | line-B | r2 | 1.6 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-003 | water-loop | r2 | 2.4 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-004 | lot-M41 | r2 | 3.0 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-005 | line-A | r2 | 0.7 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-006 | line-B | r2 | 1.4 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-007 | water-loop | r2 | 2.0 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-008 | lot-M41 | r2 | 2.8 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-009 | line-A | r2 | 0.3 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-010 | line-B | r2 | 1.1 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-011 | water-loop | r2 | 1.8 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-012 | lot-M41 | r2 | 2.5 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-013 | line-A | r2 | 3.1 | EU/mL | hold |\n| QUAL-014 | line-B | r2 | 0.8 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-015 | water-loop | r2 | 1.4 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-016 | lot-M41 | r3 | 2.1 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-017 | line-A | r3 | 2.9 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-018 | line-B | r3 | 0.5 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-019 | water-loop | r3 | 1.1 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-020 | lot-M41 | r3 | 1.9 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-021 | line-A | r3 | 2.5 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-022 | line-B | r3 | 3.2 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-023 | water-loop | r3 | 0.8 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-024 | lot-M41 | r3 | 1.6 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-025 | line-A | r3 | 2.2 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-026 | line-B | r3 | 3.0 | EU/mL | hold |\n| QUAL-027 | water-loop | r3 | 0.6 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-028 | lot-M41 | r3 | 1.2 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-029 | line-A | r3 | 1.9 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-030 | line-B | r3 | 2.6 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-031 | water-loop | r3 | 0.2 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-032 | lot-M41 | r4 | 0.9 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-033 | line-A | r4 | 1.6 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-034 | line-B | r4 | 2.4 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-035 | water-loop | r4 | 3.0 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-036 | lot-M41 | r4 | 0.7 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-037 | line-A | r4 | 1.4 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-038 | line-B | r4 | 2.0 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-039 | water-loop | r4 | 2.8 | EU/mL | hold |\n| QUAL-040 | lot-M41 | r4 | 0.3 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-041 | line-A | r4 | 1.1 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-042 | line-B | r4 | 1.8 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-043 | water-loop | r4 | 2.5 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-044 | lot-M41 | r4 | 3.1 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-045 | line-A | r4 | 0.8 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-046 | line-B | r4 | 1.4 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-047 | water-loop | r4 | 2.1 | EU/mL | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve 0.25 EU/mL, 0.50 EU/mL, both observed results, and 41 percent with their exact meanings.\nState what starts, holds, expands, and retires the lot and line controls.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","has_new_line":true,"truncated":false,"stop_type":"eos","stopping_word":"","tokens_cached":5243,"timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4234,"prompt_ms":5185.234,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.224665564478035,"prompt_per_second":816.5494556272677,"predicted_n":1010,"predicted_ms":34040.913,"predicted_per_token_ms":33.7372775024777,"predicted_per_second":29.64080311241946}},"timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4234,"prompt_ms":5185.234,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.224665564478035,"prompt_per_second":816.5494556272677,"predicted_n":1010,"predicted_ms":34040.913,"predicted_per_token_ms":33.7372775024777,"predicted_p